{"name":"Shiraz","hex":"#842833","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shiraz","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Iran, the seat of Shiraz County's Central District and the capital of Fars Province, near the remains of Persepolis.","A county of Iran, around the city."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of black grape used to make wine.","A wine made from these grapes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shiraz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shiraz","blocks":[{"text":"Shiraz is the fifth-most-populous city of Iran and the capital of Fars province, which is historically known by the exonym Persia proper. As of the 2016 national census, the population of the city was 1,565,572 people, and its built-up area with Sadra was home to almost 1,800,000 inhabitants. A census in 2021 showed an increase in the city's population to 1,995,500 people. Shiraz is located in southwestern Iran on the rudkhaneye khoshk seasonal river. The city has a moderate climate and has been a regional trade center for over a thousand years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Darvaze_Ghoran11.jpg/330px-Darvaze_Ghoran11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiraz"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Hafez_880714_095.jpg/500px-Hafez_880714_095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Hafez_880714_095.jpg/500px-Hafez_880714_095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHafez_880714_095.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Saadi_Tomb.jpg/500px-Saadi_Tomb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo